# Copy to .env and fill in the values you need.
#
# These are read from the process environment — nothing in runspace-agent
# auto-loads this file. Export it into your shell before starting the server:
#
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   runspace-srv
#
# (or use your process manager / `env $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs) runspace-srv`)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional. Parent directory of the `runspace/` workspace folder, under which
# every session's managed data lives ({RUNSPACE_DATA_DIR}/runspace/<id>/).
# When unset, the system temp directory is used. Set this to keep all session
# data in a known, persistent, easy-to-inspect location.
# RUNSPACE_DATA_DIR=~/.runspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent (Claude Code) needs credentials to reach the model. In CONTAINER
# mode the container is a clean room and does NOT inherit your shell — these
# must be passed into each POST /run request via `agent_settings.env`. The
# example scripts under examples/ read them from the environment for you.
#
# Use either an API key...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# ...or a gateway/proxy base URL + auth token:
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway.example.com
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional. Base URL of a running server, used by the scripts under examples/.
# RUNSPACE_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:6767
